## std/diagnostic.pengu — source spans, labels and Rust-style diagnostics.
##
## A general diagnostic system, not a compiler-only one: linters, validators,
## migration tools and the self-hosted LSP all need the same primitives — a
## position, a severity, an optional code, a message, and one or more marked
## ranges. `std.diagnostic` provides them with a renderer modelled on
## `rustc`/`codespan-reporting`, ANSI colour, and an LSP-compatible JSON form.
##
## ## Example
## ```pengu
## import std.diagnostic as diag
## import std.spark
##
## weave main into int:
##     var bag as DiagnosticBag is calling DiagnosticBag.new
##     defer banish bag
##     calling bag.add_source with "src/main.pengu", "var x as int is \"hello\"\n"
##
##     var span as Span is calling diag.span_from_positions with "src/main.pengu", 1, 18, 1, 25, 17, 24
##     calling bag.add with (calling diag.diagnostic with diag.Severity.Error, "E0005", "expected 'int', found 'string'", (calling diag.labels with (calling diag.label with span, "expected 'int' here", true)), (some "use '(s to int)'"))
##     var text as string is calling bag.render_colored
##     defer banish text
##     calling spark.print with text
##     return 0
## ```
##
## Output (colours omitted):
## ```text
## error[E0005]: expected 'int', found 'string'
##   --> src/main.pengu:1:18
##    |
##  1 | var x as int is "hello"
##    |                  ^^^^^^^ expected 'int' here
##    |
##    = help: use '(s to int)'
## ```
##
## ## Ownership (read this once)
## - A `Span` owns its `file` string. `span_from_positions` copies the path, so
##   the caller keeps its own string; `banish span` releases the copy.
## - `Label` owns its `Span` and its `message`. The `label` helper takes
##   ownership of the span and copies the message.
## - `Diagnostic` owns its `message`, `code`, `labels`, `help`, `note` and
##   `related`. The `diagnostic` helper copies `code`/`message`, takes ownership
##   of the label list and of the `related` list, and boxes `help`/`note`
##   copies.
## - `DiagnosticBag` owns every `Diagnostic` it holds plus the sources added
##   with `add_source`. `banish bag` releases the whole bag recursively.
## - `errors_only` / `warnings_and_errors` return **deep copies**; release the
##   list with `free_diagnostics`.
##
## ## Sources and context
## A `Span` stores only a path, never the file contents. Register the text with
## `DiagnosticBag.add_source` to get source context in the render. Without it,
## the renderer still prints the primary position and every label message, but
## no source line — which is exactly what a tool that only has positions (a
## log parser, a remote LSP client) can do.
##
## ## Complexity
## | Operation | Cost |
## |---|---|
## | `add`, `extend`, `error`, ... | O(1) amortised |
## | `len`, `is_empty`, counts | O(1) |
## | `errors_only`, `warnings_and_errors` | O(number of copied diagnostics) |
## | `render`, `render_json` | O(labels × context lines + output size) |
## | `clear` | O(items + sources) |
##
## ## Multiple labels on one line
## Each label gets its own marker row, in label order: `^^^^` for a primary
## label and `----` for a secondary one. Overlapping carets are therefore
## always readable, at the cost of one row per label. This is a deliberate
## choice (the alternative — one merged row with `|` separators — hides which
## message belongs to which range).

import std.builder
import std.json
import std.rites
import std.spark

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Module version
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

## Diagnostic module version.
const DIAGNOSTIC_VERSION as string is "2.12.0"

## LSP severity number for `Severity.Error`.
const DIAGNOSTIC_SEVERITY_ERROR as int is 1

## LSP severity number for `Severity.Warning`.
const DIAGNOSTIC_SEVERITY_WARNING as int is 2

## LSP severity number for `Severity.Info`.
const DIAGNOSTIC_SEVERITY_INFO as int is 3

## LSP severity number for `Severity.Hint`.
const DIAGNOSTIC_SEVERITY_HINT as int is 4

## ANSI reset sequence.
const DIAGNOSTIC_ANSI_RESET as string is "\x1b[0m"

## ANSI bold-red sequence (errors).
const DIAGNOSTIC_ANSI_ERROR as string is "\x1b[1;31m"

## ANSI bold-yellow sequence (warnings).
const DIAGNOSTIC_ANSI_WARNING as string is "\x1b[1;33m"

## ANSI bold-blue sequence (info).
const DIAGNOSTIC_ANSI_INFO as string is "\x1b[1;34m"

## ANSI bold-cyan sequence (hints).
const DIAGNOSTIC_ANSI_HINT as string is "\x1b[1;36m"

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Types
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

## A range in a source file.
##
## Lines and columns are **1-indexed** and columns are byte columns (the same
## convention as `std.sourcemap`), so `start_byte + start_col - 1` is exact.
## `start_byte`/`end_byte` are absolute byte offsets; they are used for
## ordering and for JSON consumers that index a buffer directly.
##
## ## Memoria
## Owns `file`; `banish span` releases it.
rune Span derive Nexus, Par, Imago:
    ## Logical path of the file (`""` for a position without a file).
    file as string
    ## 1-indexed first line.
    start_line as int
    ## 1-indexed first byte column.
    start_col as int
    ## 1-indexed line of the first byte *after* the range.
    end_line as int
    ## 1-indexed byte column just after the range.
    end_col as int
    ## Absolute byte offset of the first byte.
    start_byte as int
    ## Absolute byte offset just after the range.
    end_byte as int

## Severity of a diagnostic.
omen Severity:
    ## A program error; the tool should fail.
    Error
    ## A suspicious construct; the program is still valid.
    Warning
    ## Informational output.
    Info
    ## An optional suggestion.
    Hint

## A secondary annotation inside a diagnostic.
##
## ## Memoria
## Owns its `span` (and therefore the file path) and its `message`.
rune Label derive Nexus, Par, Imago:
    ## The marked range.
    span as Span
    ## The text printed next to the marker.
    message as string
    ## `true` renders `^^^^` (primary), `false` renders `----` (secondary).
    primary as bool

## A complete diagnostic.
##
## `labels` may be empty (a diagnostic without a position, such as "internal
## error"), and a label list without a `primary` label is treated as
## positionaless by the renderer.
##
## ## Memoria
## Owns every field; `banish d` releases the labels, messages and related list.
rune Diagnostic derive Nexus, Par, Imago:
    ## The severity.
    severity as Severity
    ## A stable code such as `"E0005"` or `"my-lint-rule"`; `""` for no code.
    code as string
    ## The headline message (no trailing period required).
    message as string
    ## Positional annotations. At most one should be primary.
    labels as list of Label
    ## An optional `help:` suggestion.
    help as maybe string
    ## An optional `note:` explanation.
    note as maybe string
    ## "See also" diagnostics.
    related as list of Diagnostic

## Render options.
rune RenderOptions derive Par:
    ## Request ANSI colour (still subject to `NO_COLOR` and TTY detection).
    color as bool
    ## Lines of context around the marked lines (default `2`).
    context_lines as int
    ## Print `note:` lines (default `true`).
    show_notes as bool
    ## Print `help:` lines (default `true`).
    show_help as bool
    ## Print `related:` lines (default `true`).
    show_related as bool
    ## Width a tab advances to when computing visual columns (default `4`).
    tab_width as int
    ## Skip `NO_COLOR`/TTY detection and honour `color` exactly (default
    ## `false`). Useful for tests and for capturing ANSI output to a file.
    force_color as bool

## A bag of diagnostics plus their counts and source texts.
##
## ## Memoria
## Owns `items` and `_sources`. `banish bag` releases everything, including the
## nested diagnostics and the copied source texts.
rune DiagnosticBag derive Nexus:
    ## The diagnostics in insertion order.
    items as list of Diagnostic
    ## Number of `Error` diagnostics (kept in sync by `add`).
    error_count as int
    ## Number of `Warning` diagnostics.
    warning_count as int
    ## Number of `Info` diagnostics.
    info_count as int
    ## Number of `Hint` diagnostics.
    hint_count as int
    ## Registered source texts, keyed by logical path.
    _sources as map of string to string

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Private C bridges
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

## Reports whether stdout is a terminal.
##
## ## Motivo
## The runtime already includes `<unistd.h>` / `<io.h>`, so the POSIX and
## Windows spellings can live in one guarded function without a new link.
##
## ## Memoria
## Reads only; no allocation.
antiquus _diagnostic_is_tty into bool:
    r"""
#ifdef _WIN32
return _isatty(_fileno(stdout)) != 0;
#else
return isatty(STDOUT_FILENO) != 0;
#endif
"""

## Number of lines in a source text (at least one).
##
## ## Motivo
## The renderer only needs line starts; keeping the line scanner here avoids a
## dependency on `std.sourcemap` (which exports its own `Span`, a name that
## would collide with this module's `Span` in a multi-module type table).
##
## ## Memoria
## Reads only; allocates nothing.
antiquus _diagnostic_line_count with s as string into int:
    r"""
if (!s.data) return 1;
int lines = 1;
for (int i = 0; i < s.len; i++) if (s.data[i] == '\n') lines++;
return lines;
"""

## Returns an owned copy of a 1-indexed line, without its terminator.
##
## ## Motivo
## Same as `_diagnostic_line_count`: one small bridge instead of importing a
## module whose `Span` has the same name as ours.
##
## ## Memoria
## Returns an owned string; release it with `banish`.
antiquus _diagnostic_line_text with s as string, line as int into string:
    r"""
if (line < 1 || !s.data) return pengu_string_from_cstr("");
int current = 1;
int start = 0;
while (current < line && start < s.len) {
    if (s.data[start] == '\n') current++;
    start++;
}
if (current < line) return pengu_string_from_cstr("");
int end = start;
while (end < s.len && s.data[end] != '\n') end++;
if (end > start && s.data[end - 1] == '\r') end--;
return pengu_string_substring(s, start, end);
"""

## Compares two strings byte-wise.
##
## ## Motivo
## General string `==` through two nested field accesses (`a.span.file ==
## b.span.file`) reaches C without the runtime helper; routing it through C
## keeps the comparison explicit and always correct.
##
## ## Memoria
## Reads only; allocates nothing.
antiquus _diagnostic_streq with a as string, b as string into bool:
    r"""
return pengu_string_equal(a, b) ? true : false;
"""

## Deep-copies a diagnostic with the derived `Imago` callback.
##
## ## Motivo
## `errors_only` and `warnings_and_errors` must return independent values; the
## derived helper is a C symbol.
##
## ## Memoria
## Returns a fully independent diagnostic; release it with `banish`.
antiquus _diagnostic_clone with d as Diagnostic into Diagnostic:
    r"""
Diagnostic out;
memset(&out, 0, sizeof out);
_pengu_clone_Diagnostic(&out, &d);
return out;
"""

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Basic constructors and helpers
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

## The strict default render options.
##
## ## Retorno
## `{color: true, context_lines: 2, show_notes: true, show_help: true,
## show_related: true, tab_width: 4, force_color: false}`.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## var opts as RenderOptions is calling diagnostic.default_render_options
## ```
weave default_render_options into RenderOptions:
    return with color is true, context_lines is 2, show_notes is true, show_help is true, show_related is true, tab_width is 4, force_color is false

## Builds a span from explicit positions.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `file`: logical path. **Copied**; the caller keeps its string.
## - `sl`, `sc`: start line and byte column (1-indexed).
## - `el`, `ec`: end line and byte column (1-indexed).
## - `sb`, `eb`: absolute start/end byte offsets.
##
## ## Retorno
## A `Span` owning a copy of `file`.
##
## ## Efectos
## Panics when `(sl, sc, sb) > (el, ec, eb)`: a reversed span is a bug in the
## caller, not something to silently swap.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## var s as Span is calling diagnostic.span_from_positions with "a.pengu", 3, 5, 3, 9, 21, 25
## ```
weave span_from_positions with file as string, sl as int, sc as int, el as int, ec as int, sb as int, eb as int into Span:
    if sl < 1 or sc < 1 or el < 1 or ec < 1:
        calling spark.panic with "span_from_positions: lines and columns are 1-indexed"
    if sb < 0 or eb < 0:
        calling spark.panic with "span_from_positions: byte offsets must be non-negative"
    if sl > el or (sl == el and sc > ec) or sb > eb:
        calling spark.panic with "span_from_positions: start position is after end position"
    var path as string is "{file}"
    return with file is path, start_line is sl, start_col is sc, end_line is el, end_col is ec, start_byte is sb, end_byte is eb

## Builds a zero-width span at one position.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `file`: logical path. Copied.
## - `line`, `col`: 1-indexed position.
## - `byte_offset`: absolute byte offset.
##
## ## Retorno
## A `Span` whose start and end are the same point.
weave span_point with file as string, line as int, col as int, byte_offset as int into Span:
    return calling span_from_positions with file, line, col, line, col, byte_offset, byte_offset

## Merges two spans into one covering both.
##
## The result keeps `a`'s file path. Merging spans from different files is
## allowed (the caller may use it to build a "from here to there" hint), but the
## renderer will group them by the result's single path; document that at the
## call site when it matters.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `a`, `b`: spans. Borrowed; the result owns a fresh copy of `a.file`.
##
## ## Retorno
## A `Span` from the earlier start to the later end.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## var both as Span is calling diagnostic.span_merge with first, second
## ```
weave span_merge with a as Span, b as Span into Span:
    var sl as int is a.start_line
    var sc as int is a.start_col
    var sb as int is a.start_byte
    var el as int is a.end_line
    var ec as int is a.end_col
    var eb as int is a.end_byte
    if b.start_line < sl or (b.start_line == sl and b.start_col < sc) or b.start_byte < sb:
        set sl is b.start_line
        set sc is b.start_col
        set sb is b.start_byte
    if b.end_line > el or (b.end_line == el and b.end_col > ec) or b.end_byte > eb:
        set el is b.end_line
        set ec is b.end_col
        set eb is b.end_byte
    return calling span_from_positions with a.file, sl, sc, el, ec, sb, eb

## Builds a label, taking ownership of `span` and copying `message`.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `span`: the range. **Ownership transfers**; do not banish it afterwards.
## - `message`: the marker text. Copied.
## - `primary`: `true` for `^^^^`, `false` for `----`.
##
## ## Retorno
## A `Label` owning the span and a copy of the message.
weave label with span as Span, message as string, primary as bool into Label:
    var text as string is "{message}"
    return with span is span, message is text, primary is primary

## Builds a label list from one label.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `one`: the label. Ownership transfers.
##
## ## Retorno
## A one-element `list of Label`.
weave labels with one as Label into list of Label:
    var out as list of Label is list of Label
    calling out.push with one
    return out

## Builds an empty label list.
##
## ## Retorno
## A `list of Label` with no elements.
weave no_labels into list of Label:
    return list of Label

## Builds an empty related list.
##
## ## Retorno
## An empty `list of Diagnostic`.
weave no_related into list of Diagnostic:
    return list of Diagnostic

## Builds a diagnostic.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `severity`: the severity.
## - `code`: a stable code; `""` for none. Copied.
## - `message`: the headline. Copied.
## - `labels`: positional annotations. **Ownership transfers.**
## - `help`: an optional suggestion. Ownership of the `maybe string` transfers.
## - `note`: an optional explanation. Ownership transfers.
## - `related`: see-also diagnostics. Ownership transfers.
##
## ## Retorno
## A `Diagnostic` owning all of the above.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## var d as Diagnostic is calling diagnostic.diagnostic with diagnostic.Severity.Warning, "lint/no-shadow", "shadows an outer binding", (calling diagnostic.labels with (calling diagnostic.label with s, "shadowed here", true)), (maybe none), (maybe none), (calling diagnostic.no_related)
## ```
weave diagnostic with severity as Severity, code as string, message as string, labels_list as list of Label, help as maybe string, note as maybe string, related as list of Diagnostic into Diagnostic:
    var code_copy as string is "{code}"
    var msg_copy as string is "{message}"
    return with severity is severity, code is code_copy, message is msg_copy, labels is labels_list, help is help, note is note, related is related

## Releases every diagnostic of a list, then the list itself.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `items`: an owned `list of Diagnostic` (typically from `errors_only`).
##
## ## Retorno
## Nothing.
##
## ## Memoria
## Releases each diagnostic recursively, then the list buffer.
weave free_diagnostics with items as list of Diagnostic into void:
    var i as int is 0
    while i < items.len:
        banish items at i
        set i is i + 1
    banish items

## Returns the LSP numeric severity (1 error, 2 warning, 3 info, 4 hint).
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `sev`: a severity.
##
## ## Retorno
## `1..4`.
weave severity_number with sev as Severity into int:
    if sev == Severity.Error:
        return DIAGNOSTIC_SEVERITY_ERROR
    if sev == Severity.Warning:
        return DIAGNOSTIC_SEVERITY_WARNING
    if sev == Severity.Info:
        return DIAGNOSTIC_SEVERITY_INFO
    return DIAGNOSTIC_SEVERITY_HINT

## Returns the lowercase severity name.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `sev`: a severity.
##
## ## Retorno
## `"error"`, `"warning"`, `"info"` or `"hint"`.
weave severity_name with sev as Severity into string:
    if sev == Severity.Error:
        return "error"
    if sev == Severity.Warning:
        return "warning"
    if sev == Severity.Info:
        return "info"
    return "hint"

## Returns the ANSI prefix for a severity.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `sev`: a severity.
##
## ## Retorno
## One of the `DIAGNOSTIC_ANSI_*` constants.
weave severity_color with sev as Severity into string:
    if sev == Severity.Error:
        return DIAGNOSTIC_ANSI_ERROR
    if sev == Severity.Warning:
        return DIAGNOSTIC_ANSI_WARNING
    if sev == Severity.Info:
        return DIAGNOSTIC_ANSI_INFO
    return DIAGNOSTIC_ANSI_HINT

enchanting DiagnosticBag:
    ## Constructs an empty bag.
    ##
    ## ## Retorno
    ## A bag with no diagnostics, zero counters and no sources.
    ##
    ## ## Memoria
    ## O(1); release it with `banish`.
    weave ritual new into DiagnosticBag:
        return with items is list of Diagnostic, error_count is 0, warning_count is 0, info_count is 0, hint_count is 0, _sources is map of string to string

    ## Adds a diagnostic, taking ownership of it.
    ##
    ## ## Parámetros
    ## - `d`: the diagnostic. Ownership transfers to the bag.
    ##
    ## ## Efectos
    ## Increments the matching severity counter.
    weave add with d as Diagnostic into void:
        calling self->items.push with d
        if d.severity == Severity.Error:
            set self->error_count is self->error_count + 1
        else if d.severity == Severity.Warning:
            set self->warning_count is self->warning_count + 1
        else if d.severity == Severity.Info:
            set self->info_count is self->info_count + 1
        else:
            set self->hint_count is self->hint_count + 1

    ## Adds every diagnostic of a list, taking ownership of the elements.
    ##
    ## The source list buffer is left empty but still allocated: `banish` it
    ## after the call (the elements now belong to the bag).
    ##
    ## ## Parámetros
    ## - `ds`: diagnostics. Element ownership transfers.
    weave extend with ds as list of Diagnostic into void:
        for d in ds:
            calling self.add with d
        calling ds.clear

    ## Adds an `Error` diagnostic with one primary label.
    ##
    ## ## Parámetros
    ## - `message`: the headline. Copied.
    ## - `span`: the position. Ownership transfers to the label.
    weave error with message as string, span as Span into void:
        var lb as Label is calling label with span, "", true
        var d as Diagnostic is calling diagnostic with Severity.Error, "", message, (calling labels with lb), (maybe none), (maybe none), (calling no_related)
        calling self.add with d

    ## Adds a `Warning` diagnostic with one primary label.
    ##
    ## ## Parámetros
    ## - `message`: the headline. Copied.
    ## - `span`: the position. Ownership transfers.
    weave warning with message as string, span as Span into void:
        var lb as Label is calling label with span, "", true
        var d as Diagnostic is calling diagnostic with Severity.Warning, "", message, (calling labels with lb), (maybe none), (maybe none), (calling no_related)
        calling self.add with d

    ## Adds an `Info` diagnostic with one primary label.
    ##
    ## ## Parámetros
    ## - `message`: the headline. Copied.
    ## - `span`: the position. Ownership transfers.
    weave info with message as string, span as Span into void:
        var lb as Label is calling label with span, "", true
        var d as Diagnostic is calling diagnostic with Severity.Info, "", message, (calling labels with lb), (maybe none), (maybe none), (calling no_related)
        calling self.add with d

    ## Adds a `Hint` diagnostic with one primary label.
    ##
    ## ## Parámetros
    ## - `message`: the headline. Copied.
    ## - `span`: the position. Ownership transfers.
    weave hint with message as string, span as Span into void:
        var lb as Label is calling label with span, "", true
        var d as Diagnostic is calling diagnostic with Severity.Hint, "", message, (calling labels with lb), (maybe none), (maybe none), (calling no_related)
        calling self.add with d

    ## Registers the source text of `file`, copying both strings.
    ##
    ## Re-registering the same path replaces the previous text.
    ##
    ## ## Parámetros
    ## - `file`: logical path. Borrowed; copied.
    ## - `text`: file contents. Borrowed; copied.
    weave add_source with file as string, text as string into void:
        var k as string is "{file}"
        var v as string is "{text}"
        calling self->_sources.put with k, v

    ## Adds the contents of `path` after the caller has read them.
    ##
    ## This is a convenience alias of `add_source`; the module never touches the
    ## filesystem itself, so a remote LSP client can register in-memory buffers.
    ##
    ## ## Parámetros
    ## - `file`: logical path used by spans. Copied.
    ## - `text`: source text. Copied.
    weave source with file as string, text as string into void:
        calling self.add_source with file, text

    ## Number of diagnostics.
    weave len into int:
        return self->items.len

    ## True when the bag has no diagnostics.
    weave is_empty into bool:
        return self->items.len == 0

    ## True when at least one diagnostic is an `Error`.
    weave has_errors into bool:
        return self->error_count > 0

    ## True when at least one diagnostic is a `Warning`.
    weave has_warnings into bool:
        return self->warning_count > 0

    ## Counts the diagnostics of one severity.
    ##
    ## ## Parámetros
    ## - `sev`: the severity to count.
    ##
    ## ## Retorno
    ## The matching stored counter.
    weave count_by_severity with sev as Severity into int:
        if sev == Severity.Error:
            return self->error_count
        if sev == Severity.Warning:
            return self->warning_count
        if sev == Severity.Info:
            return self->info_count
        return self->hint_count

    ## Deep copies of every `Error` diagnostic, in insertion order.
    ##
    ## ## Retorno
    ## An owned `list of Diagnostic`; release it with `free_diagnostics`.
    weave errors_only into list of Diagnostic:
        var out as list of Diagnostic is list of Diagnostic
        for d in self->items:
            if d.severity == Severity.Error:
                calling out.push with (calling _diagnostic_clone with d)
        return out

    ## Deep copies of every `Warning` and `Error`, in insertion order.
    ##
    ## ## Retorno
    ## An owned `list of Diagnostic`; release it with `free_diagnostics`.
    weave warnings_and_errors into list of Diagnostic:
        var out as list of Diagnostic is list of Diagnostic
        for d in self->items:
            if d.severity == Severity.Error or d.severity == Severity.Warning:
                calling out.push with (calling _diagnostic_clone with d)
        return out

    ## Removes every diagnostic and every registered source.
    ##
    ## ## Memoria
    ## Releases the nested diagnostics and the source copies; the bag remains
    ## usable.
    weave clear into void:
        var i as int is 0
        while i < self->items.len:
            banish self->items at i
            set i is i + 1
        calling self->items.clear
        var smap as map of string to string is self->_sources
        for k in smap:
            var v as string is smap at k
            banish k
            banish v
        calling self->_sources.clear
        set self->error_count is 0
        set self->warning_count is 0
        set self->info_count is 0
        set self->hint_count is 0

    ## True when `file` has a registered source.
    ##
    ## ## Parámetros
    ## - `file`: logical path. Borrowed.
    weave has_source with file as string into bool:
        var smap as map of string to string is self->_sources
        return calling smap.contains with file

    ## The registered source text as an owned copy.
    ##
    ## ## Parámetros
    ## - `file`: logical path. Borrowed.
    ##
    ## ## Retorno
    ## `some text` (an owned copy; release it with `banish`) or `none`.
    weave source_of with file as string into maybe string:
        var smap as map of string to string is self->_sources
        if calling smap.contains with file:
            var borrowed as string is smap at file
            var text_copy as string is "{borrowed}"
            return some text_copy
        return maybe none

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Render helpers
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

## Number of decimal digits in a non-negative integer.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `n`: a value `>= 0`.
##
## ## Retorno
## At least `1`.
weave _digits with n as int into int:
    var v as int is n
    if v < 0:
        set v is -v
    var d as int is 1
    while v >= 10:
        set v is v / 10
        set d is d + 1
    return d

## Visual column of a byte column inside one line.
##
## Tabs advance to the next multiple of `tab_width`; a multibyte UTF-8
## codepoint counts as one column (its continuation bytes count as zero). This
## is what makes a caret line up under `ñ` or an emoji even though `Span`
## columns are byte offsets.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `line`: the line text (no trailing `\n`).
## - `byte_col`: number of bytes before the target column.
## - `tab_width`: tab stop width.
##
## ## Retorno
## A non-negative visual column.
weave _visual_col with line as string, byte_col as int, tab_width as int into int:
    var n as int is line length
    var limit as int is byte_col
    if limit < 0:
        set limit is 0
    if limit > n:
        set limit is n
    var raw as ref to frozen byte is bytes of line
    var i as int is 0
    var col as int is 0
    while i < limit:
        var b as int is (raw at i) to int
        if b == 9:
            set col is col + (tab_width - (col % tab_width))
        else if (b & 192) == 128:
            # UTF-8 continuation byte: the codepoint was already counted at
            # its lead byte.
            set col is col
        else:
            set col is col + 1
        set i is i + 1
    return col

## Visual width of a byte range inside one line.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `line`: the line text.
## - `start_byte`: first byte offset in the line.
## - `end_byte`: one past the last byte offset in the line.
## - `tab_width`: tab stop width.
##
## ## Retorno
## At least `1`, so a zero-width point still gets one caret.
weave _visual_width with line as string, start_byte as int, end_byte as int, tab_width as int into int:
    var a as int is calling _visual_col with line, start_byte, tab_width
    var b as int is calling _visual_col with line, end_byte, tab_width
    if b <= a:
        return 1
    return b - a

## True when a `list of string` contains `needle`.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `xs`: strings to scan. Borrowed.
## - `needle`: the value to find. Borrowed.
weave _has_string with xs as list of string, needle as string into bool:
    for x in xs:
        if x == needle:
            return true
    return false

## Appends an empty-gutter separator row (`   |`).
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `sb`: destination builder. Mutated.
## - `gutter`: width of the line-number column.
weave _gutter_row with sb as ref to StringBuilder, gutter as int into void:
    calling sb.append_spaces with gutter
    calling sb.append with " |"
    calling sb.append_char with (10 to char)

## Appends one labelled marker row for a span.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `sb`: destination builder. Mutated.
## - `gutter`: width of the line-number column.
## - `line_text`: the source line. Borrowed.
## - `label`: the annotation. Borrowed.
## - `end_col`: exclusive end byte column in the line (1-indexed).
## - `opts`: render options.
weave _marker_row with sb as ref to StringBuilder, gutter as int, line_text as string, label as Label, end_col as int, opts as RenderOptions into void:
    calling sb.append_spaces with gutter
    calling sb.append with " | "
    var pad as int is calling _visual_col with line_text, (label.span.start_col - 1), opts.tab_width
    calling sb.append_spaces with pad
    var width as int is calling _visual_width with line_text, (label.span.start_col - 1), (end_col - 1), opts.tab_width
    var mark as string is "-"
    if label.primary:
        set mark is "^"
    calling sb.append_repeat with mark, width
    if (label.message length) > 0:
        calling sb.append with " "
        calling sb.append with label.message
    calling sb.append_char with (10 to char)

## Renders one file group of a diagnostic.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `bag`: the bag (for registered sources). Borrowed.
## - `group`: labels sharing one file. Borrowed.
## - `opts`: render options.
## - `color`: effective colour flag (only used by the caller's header).
## - `sb`: destination builder. Mutated.
weave _render_group with bag as ref to DiagnosticBag, group as list of Label, opts as RenderOptions, color as bool, sb as ref to StringBuilder into void:
    if group.len == 0:
        return
    var head_label as Label is group at 0
    var file as string is head_label.span.file
    calling sb.append with "  --> "
    if (file length) == 0:
        calling sb.append with "<unknown>"
    else:
        calling sb.append with file
    calling sb.append_char with ':'
    calling sb.append_int with head_label.span.start_line
    calling sb.append_char with ':'
    calling sb.append_int with head_label.span.start_col
    calling sb.append_char with (10 to char)

    var smap as map of string to string is bag->_sources
    if not calling smap.contains with file:
        # No source text: print the labels as plain positions. This is the
        # documented behaviour for remote/position-only diagnostics.
        for lb in group:
            if (lb.message length) > 0:
                calling sb.append with "   = "
                calling sb.append_int with lb.span.start_line
                calling sb.append_char with ':'
                calling sb.append_int with lb.span.start_col
                calling sb.append with ": "
                calling sb.append with lb.message
                calling sb.append_char with (10 to char)
        return

    var source as string is smap at file
    var line_count as int is calling _diagnostic_line_count with source
    var min_line as int is head_label.span.start_line
    var max_line as int is head_label.span.end_line
    for lb in group:
        if lb.span.start_line < min_line:
            set min_line is lb.span.start_line
        if lb.span.end_line > max_line:
            set max_line is lb.span.end_line
    var from_line as int is min_line - opts.context_lines
    if from_line < 1:
        set from_line is 1
    var to_line as int is max_line + opts.context_lines
    if to_line > line_count:
        set to_line is line_count
    # A trailing newline makes the line scanner report one empty last line; showing
    # it as context is noise, so trim empty lines *after* the last labelled
    # line. (Empty lines between labels are kept.)
    var trimming as bool is true
    while trimming and to_line > max_line:
        var tail as string is calling _diagnostic_line_text with source, to_line
        if (tail length) == 0:
            set to_line is to_line - 1
        else:
            set trimming is false
        banish tail

    var gutter as int is calling _digits with max_line
    calling _gutter_row with sb, gutter
    var line as int is from_line
    while line <= to_line:
        var text as string is calling _diagnostic_line_text with source, line
        var padlen as int is gutter - (calling _digits with line)
        calling sb.append_spaces with padlen
        calling sb.append_int with line
        calling sb.append with " | "
        calling sb.append with text
        calling sb.append_char with (10 to char)
        for lb in group:
            if lb.span.start_line == line:
                var end_col as int is lb.span.end_col
                if lb.span.end_line != line:
                    set end_col is (text length) + 1
                calling _marker_row with sb, gutter, text, lb, end_col, opts
        banish text
        set line is line + 1
    calling _gutter_row with sb, gutter

## Renders one diagnostic (header, groups, notes, related).
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `bag`: the bag (for sources). Borrowed.
## - `d`: the diagnostic. Borrowed.
## - `opts`: render options.
## - `color`: effective colour flag.
## - `sb`: destination builder. Mutated.
weave _render_one with bag as ref to DiagnosticBag, d as Diagnostic, opts as RenderOptions, color as bool, sb as ref to StringBuilder into void:
    var sev_name as string is calling severity_name with d.severity
    if color:
        calling sb.append with (calling severity_color with d.severity)
    calling sb.append with sev_name
    if color:
        calling sb.append with DIAGNOSTIC_ANSI_RESET
    if (d.code length) > 0:
        calling sb.append with "["
        calling sb.append with d.code
        calling sb.append with "]"
    calling sb.append with ": "
    calling sb.append with d.message
    calling sb.append_char with (10 to char)

    var has_primary as bool is false
    for lb in d.labels:
        if lb.primary:
            set has_primary is true
    if not has_primary:
        for lb in d.labels:
            calling sb.append with "   = "
            calling sb.append_int with lb.span.start_line
            calling sb.append_char with ':'
            calling sb.append_int with lb.span.start_col
            if (lb.message length) > 0:
                calling sb.append with ": "
                calling sb.append with lb.message
            calling sb.append_char with (10 to char)
    else:
        var seen as list of string is list of string
        for probe in d.labels:
            if not calling _has_string with seen, probe.span.file:
                var group as list of Label is list of Label
                for other in d.labels:
                    if calling _diagnostic_streq with other.span.file, probe.span.file:
                        calling group.push with other
                calling _render_group with bag, group, opts, color, sb
                calling seen.push with probe.span.file
                banish group
        banish seen

    if opts.show_notes and d.note.is_present:
        calling sb.append with "   = note: "
        calling sb.append with d.note.value
        calling sb.append_char with (10 to char)
    if opts.show_help and d.help.is_present:
        calling sb.append with "   = help: "
        calling sb.append with d.help.value
        calling sb.append_char with (10 to char)
    if opts.show_related:
        for r in d.related:
            calling sb.append with "   = related: "
            calling sb.append with r.message
            if r.labels.len > 0:
                let rl is r.labels at 0
                calling sb.append with " ("
                calling sb.append with rl.span.file
                calling sb.append_char with ':'
                calling sb.append_int with rl.span.start_line
                calling sb.append_char with ':'
                calling sb.append_int with rl.span.start_col
                calling sb.append with ")"
            calling sb.append_char with (10 to char)

    ## Returns the main span of a diagnostic (first primary label), or a zero
## span when it has no positional label.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `d`: the diagnostic. Borrowed.
##
## ## Retorno
## The primary `Span`, possibly `{file:"", line:1, col:1, ...}`.
weave _main_span with d as Diagnostic into Span:
    for lb in d.labels:
        if lb.primary:
            return lb.span
    if d.labels.len > 0:
        return (d.labels at 0).span
    return calling span_point with "", 1, 1, 0

## True when colour should be used for `requested`.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `requested`: the caller's colour preference.
##
## ## Retorno
## `false` when `requested` is false, when `NO_COLOR` is set, or when stdout is
## not a TTY; `true` otherwise.
weave _color_enabled with requested as bool into bool:
    if not requested:
        return false
    var nc as maybe string is calling rites.getenv with "NO_COLOR"
    var has_nc as bool is nc.is_present
    banish nc
    if has_nc:
        return false
    return calling _diagnostic_is_tty

enchanting DiagnosticBag:
    ## Renders every diagnostic with explicit options.
    ##
    ## ## Parámetros
    ## - `opts`: render options.
    ##
    ## ## Retorno
    ## An owned string (each diagnostic is separated by a blank line). Release
    ## it with `banish`.
    ##
    ## ## Efectos
    ## Colour is used only when `opts.color` is true **and** `opts.force_color`
    ## is true, or when `opts.color` is true and stdout is a TTY with
    ## `NO_COLOR` unset.
    weave render with opts as RenderOptions into string:
        var eff as bool is false
        if opts.force_color:
            set eff is opts.color
        else:
            set eff is calling _color_enabled with opts.color
        var sb as StringBuilder is calling StringBuilder.new
        defer banish sb
        for d in self->items:
            calling _render_one with self, d, opts, eff, sigil of sb
            calling sb.append_char with (10 to char)
        return calling sb.finish

    ## Renders every diagnostic without colour.
    ##
    ## ## Retorno
    ## An owned string; release it with `banish`.
    weave render_plain into string:
        var opts as RenderOptions is calling default_render_options
        set opts.color is false
        set opts.force_color is false
        return calling self.render with opts

    ## Renders every diagnostic with ANSI colour, honouring `NO_COLOR` and TTY
    ## detection.
    ##
    ## ## Retorno
    ## An owned string; release it with `banish`.
    weave render_colored into string:
        var opts as RenderOptions is calling default_render_options
        set opts.color is true
        set opts.force_color is false
        return calling self.render with opts

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LSP-compatible JSON
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

## Builds an LSP `Position` object from a 1-indexed `(line, col)`.
##
## LSP positions are 0-indexed. `character` is a byte column, matching
## `Span.start_col`/`end_col`; clients that need UTF-16 code units can convert
## with the source text.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `line`: 1-indexed line.
## - `col`: 1-indexed byte column.
##
## ## Retorno
## An owned `JsonValue` object; the caller releases the containing tree.
weave _lsp_position with line as int, col as int into JsonValue:
    var o as JsonValue is calling JsonValue.empty_object
    var l as int is line - 1
    var c as int is col - 1
    if l < 0:
        set l is 0
    if c < 0:
        set c is 0
    calling o.put_json with "line", (calling JsonValue.int_val with (l to i64))
    calling o.put_json with "character", (calling JsonValue.int_val with (c to i64))
    return o

## Builds an LSP `Range` object from a span.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `span`: the source span. Borrowed.
##
## ## Retorno
## An owned `JsonValue` object.
weave _lsp_range with span as Span into JsonValue:
    var o as JsonValue is calling JsonValue.empty_object
    calling o.put_json with "start", (calling _lsp_position with span.start_line, span.start_col)
    calling o.put_json with "end", (calling _lsp_position with span.end_line, span.end_col)
    return o

## Builds an LSP `Location` object.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `file`: logical path. Borrowed.
## - `span`: the range inside `file`. Borrowed.
##
## ## Retorno
## An owned `JsonValue` object.
weave _lsp_location with file as string, span as Span into JsonValue:
    var o as JsonValue is calling JsonValue.empty_object
    var uri as string is "file://{file}"
    calling o.put_json with "uri", (calling JsonValue.string_val with uri)
    calling o.put_json with "range", (calling _lsp_range with span)
    return o

## Builds one LSP `Diagnostic` object.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `d`: the diagnostic. Borrowed.
##
## ## Retorno
## An owned `JsonValue` object.
weave _lsp_diagnostic with d as Diagnostic into JsonValue:
    var o as JsonValue is calling JsonValue.empty_object
    var main_span as Span is calling _main_span with d
    calling o.put_json with "range", (calling _lsp_range with main_span)
    calling o.put_json with "severity", (calling JsonValue.int_val with ((calling severity_number with d.severity) to i64))
    if (d.code length) > 0:
        var code_copy as string is "{d.code}"
        calling o.put_json with "code", (calling JsonValue.string_val with code_copy)
    var source_copy as string is "pengu"
    calling o.put_json with "source", (calling JsonValue.string_val with source_copy)
    var msg_copy as string is "{d.message}"
    calling o.put_json with "message", (calling JsonValue.string_val with msg_copy)

    var related as JsonValue is calling JsonValue.empty_array
    var main_seen as bool is false
    for lb in d.labels:
        var is_main as bool is false
        if lb.primary and not main_seen:
            set is_main is true
            set main_seen is true
        if not is_main:
            var ri as JsonValue is calling JsonValue.empty_object
            calling ri.put_json with "location", (calling _lsp_location with lb.span.file, lb.span)
            var lmsg as string is "{lb.message}"
            calling ri.put_json with "message", (calling JsonValue.string_val with lmsg)
            calling related.push_json with ri
    for r in d.related:
        var ri2 as JsonValue is calling JsonValue.empty_object
        var rmain as Span is calling _main_span with r
        calling ri2.put_json with "location", (calling _lsp_location with rmain.file, rmain)
        var rmsg as string is "{r.message}"
        calling ri2.put_json with "message", (calling JsonValue.string_val with rmsg)
        calling related.push_json with ri2
    if calling related.array_len > 0:
        calling o.put_json with "relatedInformation", related
    else:
        banish related
    return o

enchanting DiagnosticBag:
    ## Renders every diagnostic as a JSON array of LSP `Diagnostic` objects.
    ##
    ## Each object has `range`, `severity`, an optional `code`, `source:
    ## "pengu"`, `message`, and `relatedInformation` when there are secondary
    ## labels or `related` diagnostics. Positions are 0-indexed. An empty bag
    ## renders as `[]`.
    ##
    ## ## Retorno
    ## An owned JSON string; release it with `banish`.
    ##
    ## ## Ejemplo
    ## ```pengu
    ## var payload as string is calling bag.render_json
    ## defer banish payload
    ## ```
    weave render_json into string:
        var arr as JsonValue is calling JsonValue.empty_array
        for d in self->items:
            calling arr.push_json with (calling _lsp_diagnostic with d)
        var text as string is calling json.stringify with arr
        banish arr
        return text
